{"title":"2002 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 8","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In a jar, the ratio of the number of oatmeal cookies to the number of chocolate chip cookies is 5:2. If there are 20 oatmeal cookies, the number of chocolate chip cookies in the jar is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/f/eaf5c80356d89f0218ffa4c37710256b1d715979.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 28 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 50 \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 8 \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 12 \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"387\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Using the ratio, we can let the number of oatmeal cookies be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/e/87e9f9eb8f39820b3b8cd2c4b06e10d90e0d3b44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5x$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" /> and the number of chocolate chip cookies be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/c/2ec701493fa72dda5d6747fe14f30e7b1c2fb6c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" />. Since the number of oatmeal cookies is also <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/2/08265224f11a0d7649c50e33e6d4715946f4177a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5x = 20$\" width=\"61\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/7/ea768618848c1aea8a32490c327911e8ab7243a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Plugging <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/7/ea768618848c1aea8a32490c327911e8ab7243a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/c/2ec701493fa72dda5d6747fe14f30e7b1c2fb6c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" /> to find the number of chocolate chip cookies, we find that there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/1/c11830d82e09ea0bffac0ea92fa104125cffc98b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\times 4 = \\boxed {\\textbf {(C) } 8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"122\" height=\"30\" /> chocolate chip cookies.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)\" title=\"2002 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)\">2002 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2002 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2002 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" 